@page "/components/accordionlist"
@inherits AppComponentBase

@using Bit.BlazorUI.Demo.Client.Core.Pages.Components.Extras.AccordionList

<PageOutlet Url="components/accordionlist"
            Title="AccordionList"
            Description="BitAccordionList renders a list of expandable BitAccordion items from a single collection and owns their expand/collapse state, in single- or multiple-expand mode, with bound keys, cancellable toggles and keyboard navigation." />

<div>
    <DemoPage Name="AccordionList"
              SecondaryNames="@(["ExpanderList, Expander, Accordion"])"
              Description="BitAccordionList renders a list of expandable BitAccordion items from a single collection and owns their expand/collapse state - in single-expand mode by default, or in multiple-expand mode with an optional ceiling on how many panels stay open - with two-way bound keys, keyboard navigation between the headers, per-item icons, actions and templates, and cancellable toggles."
              Parameters="componentParameters"
              SubClasses="componentSubClasses"
              SubEnums="componentSubEnums"
              PublicMembers="componentPublicMembers"
              GitHubExtrasUrl="AccordionList/BitAccordionList.razor"
              GitHubDemoUrl="Extras/AccordionList/BitAccordionListDemo.razor">
        <NotesTemplate>
            <BitText>
                To use this component, you need to install the
                <BitLink Href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Bit.BlazorUI.Extras" Target="_blank">
                    <BitTag Reversed
                            Text="Bit.BlazorUI.Extras"
                            Color="BitColor.SecondaryBackground"
                            IconName="@BitIconName.NavigateExternalInline" />
                </BitLink>
                nuget package, as described in the Optional steps of the
                <BitLink Href="/getting-started">Getting started</BitLink> page.
            </BitText>
            <br />
            <BitText>
                The BitAccordionList is a <BitTag Color="BitColor.SecondaryBackground">Multi-API</BitTag> component
                which can accept the list of Items in 3 different ways:
                <br />
                1. The <BitLink Href="#accordion-list-item"><BitTag Color="BitColor.SecondaryBackground">BitAccordionListItem</BitTag></BitLink> class <br />
                2. A <BitTag Color="BitColor.SecondaryBackground">Custom Generic</BitTag> class <br />
                3. The <BitLink Href="#accordion-list-option"><BitTag Color="BitColor.SecondaryBackground">BitAccordionListOption</BitTag></BitLink> component
            </BitText>
        </NotesTemplate>
        <DescriptionTemplate>
            BitAccordionList is a sugar component over the single-item <BitLink Href="/components/accordion">BitAccordion</BitLink>:
            instead of wiring several accordions together by hand, you hand it one collection and it renders an item for each
            entry and owns the expand/collapse state of all of them - one panel at a time by default, or several at once with
            <code>Multiple</code>. That state can be left to the component, seeded with <code>DefaultExpandedKey(s)</code>,
            two-way bound through <code>ExpandedKey(s)</code>, or driven from code with <code>Expand</code>,
            <code>Collapse</code>, <code>Toggle</code>, <code>ExpandAll</code> and <code>CollapseAll</code>, while
            <code>MaxExpanded</code> caps how many panels stay open at once and <code>OnToggling</code> can refuse a change
            before it happens. Everything a single accordion can do is set once for the whole list and overridden per item
            where it matters - the icons, the size, the colors, the templates, the actions beside a header, how the panels
            are rendered - and the headers answer the arrow, Home and End keys on top of Tab, as the WAI-ARIA accordion
            pattern offers.
        </DescriptionTemplate>
        <Examples>
            <BitPivot Classes="@(new() { HeaderContainer = "pivot-sticky-header" })" MountAll="RenderForMcpClient">
                <BitPivotItem HeaderText="Item">
                    <_BitAccordionListItemDemo />
                </BitPivotItem>

                <BitPivotItem HeaderText="Custom">
                    <_BitAccordionListCustomDemo />
                </BitPivotItem>

                <BitPivotItem HeaderText="Option">
                    <_BitAccordionListOptionDemo />
                </BitPivotItem>
            </BitPivot>
        </Examples>
    </DemoPage>
</div>
